<title>UK: Brown says next budget will be in Spring 1998.</title>
<headline>Brown says next budget will be in Spring 1998.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said on Wednesday that he would not be presenting another budget until the Spring of 1998.</p>
<p>The former Conservative government held its last budget in November but the Labour Party pledged to hold another within two months of taking power at the May 1 election so that it could cut VAT on domestic fuel and introduce a windfall tax on privatised utility companies.</p>
<p>-- Cheryl Juckes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
